{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"45246929f529e7885396de70717efbc89f97997c7ce2402f0e6a9404661ebb05","digest":{"component_or_area":"status-mapping tests / outbound mapper","key_entities":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_status_mapping.py","_DRIFT_WARNED","resolve_outbound_status","outbound_mapper.reset_drift_warnings()","test_unmapped_status_drifts","test_drift_warning_deduped_within_pass"],"problem_keywords":["test isolation","shared mutable state","dedupe cache","test order dependency","pytest fixture"],"propositions":["Process-global _DRIFT_WARNED set in outbound_mapper suppresses duplicate drift warnings, causing test order dependencies when warnings are asserted.","Status-mapping tests do not reset _DRIFT_WARNED between test runs, allowing earlier tests to pollute later tests that assert drift warnings are emitted.","Adding an autouse pytest fixture that calls outbound_mapper.reset_drift_warnings() before each test isolates _DRIFT_WARNED state and eliminates test order dependency.","Order-independence of drift-warning assertions is verifiable by a two-part oracle test that would fail (RED) without the fixture and pass (GREEN) with it."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787444540170757001,"uuid":"24035e7e-3652-45a4-8e34-0b726590c73f"}